# Build context allowlist.
#
# Everything is excluded, then the paths the Dockerfiles actually ADD are
# re-included. Same reasoning as BUNDLE_ONLY in docs/HARDENING.md §2.2: a
# denylist fails open (forget to add a line, junk ships silently), an allowlist
# fails closed and loudly (forget a line, the build errors on a missing path).
#
# Two Dockerfiles share this context:
#   Dockerfile             — the app image (docker-compose.yml, Steerfile)
#   docker/unit/Dockerfile — the all-in-one test image (docker-compose.unit.yml)
#
# If you add an ADD/COPY line to either, add the path here too or the build
# will fail with "failed to compute cache key: not found".

*

# --- files ADDed to /srv ---------------------------------------------------
!Gemfile
!Gemfile.lock
!Rakefile
!package.json
!config.ru
!.rspec
!.rubocop.yml
!.rubocop_todo.yml

# --- directories ADDed to /srv ---------------------------------------------
!app
!bin
!config
!db
!lib
!log
!public
!spec
!vendor

# docker/unit/{start.sh,waitpg.sh,waitredis.sh,Procfile} for the unit image
!docker

# --- re-excluded from within the above -------------------------------------

# Decrypts config/credentials.yml.enc. Gitignored, so CI never has it, but a
# developer building locally would otherwise bake their key into the image.
# Pass RAILS_MASTER_KEY at runtime instead.
config/master.key

# Local runtime droppings that would bust the layer cache on every build.
log/*.log
public/assets
**/.DS_Store

# Note: spec/ is intentionally still included, because Dockerfile has
# `ADD spec /srv/spec`. Removing the test suite from the runtime image is step
# 1 of docs/HARDENING.md — delete that ADD line and the !spec above together.
